# Keep the build context small. `docker/Dockerfile` does `COPY . .` twice
# (planner + builder) and the release job builds for two platforms, so anything
# left here is transferred four times.
#
# NOTE: .dockerignore patterns use Go filepath.Match — `*` does not cross `/`,
# so `*.key` would only match the repo root. Use `**/` where nesting matters.
target/
target-linux/

.git/
.github/

# The base image (rust:${RUST_VERSION}-alpine) IS the toolchain pin. Letting
# rust-toolchain.toml (channel = "stable") into the context makes `cargo build`
# resolve a different rustc than `cargo chef cook` did — different fingerprints,
# so the whole cooked dependency layer including RocksDB is discarded.
#
# Do NOT "fix" that with ENV RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=${RUST_VERSION}: the image
# installs the toolchain under its full three-part name (1.94.1), so asking for
# "1.94" makes rustup download a redundant second toolchain in every stage.
rust-toolchain.toml

# Never bake keys or local chain state into an image layer.
**/*.key
# Crash leftovers from write_secret_file: `COPY . .` runs twice, so one of
# these would be baked into an image layer.
**/.*.tmp[0-9]*.[0-9]*
data/
devnet-data/
.karoowa/

# Local scratch (see .gitignore).
files/
scratch/
.claude/
.cursor/

docs/
specs/
*.md
!README.md

**/.DS_Store
lcov.info
